{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA store write that cannot acquire the write lock in its budget is DISCARDED — no retry, no spool.\n`acquire()` computes `total_wait = timeout * attempts` into **one** deadline\n(`_store/lock.py:695-698`), so `attempts` is a silent multiplier, not a retry loop. Both legs\nnon-blocking-poll with jitter (`lock.py:215`, `lock.py:628`), so there is no fairness.\n\nRe-measured 2026-08-11 against an APFS clone of the live 737M tracker (full numbers in the AC#1\ncomment):\n\n* **The 6-writer storm no longer loses writes** — 6/6, 16/16, 48/48 concurrent `rebar comment`s\n  all succeed. 7084's hold-duration fixes were real.\n* **Loss is still reachable and terminal, now driven by HOLDER DURATION.** A 70s holder + 3\n  comments → 3/3 exit 1 and **0 of 3 markers present afterwards**. A 45s holder + one `rebar\n  claim` → fails at exactly **30.30s** (`attempts=1`). A 40s holder left 6 comments succeeding at\n  **59.5s of a 60s budget**.\n\nField-confirmed: the live Jira DC CI run recorded here spent the 30s budget on an ordinary\nrunner, and the lost write broke the reconciler's idempotency invariant.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Bounded retry-with-backoff, not fair queueing.** When one holder outlives the whole budget every\nwaiter fails regardless of service order, so FIFO buys nothing against the measured failure.\nBounded re-attempts convert loss into latency with less machinery than a queue.\n\nRetry is safe without the phantom-write semantics that got R6 (spool-and-adopt) declined on 7084,\nbecause **the retry lives strictly inside `acquire()`**: it re-attempts only the acquisition, and\n`LockTimeout` is raised before the caller's write body has run. Once `acquire()` returns, the loop\nis finished and cannot re-enter, so no write is ever replayed and nothing becomes\nvisible-but-uncommitted. A retry at any layer above the lock WOULD risk a duplicate append; that\nboundary is asserted by test, not merely claimed in prose.\n\nChecked against the \"error surfaced but the write had landed\" shape: one `transition` takes up to\nsix acquisitions, five of them AFTER the STATUS commit (signature `transition_close.py:433`, links,\naudit comment, compaction, push). Each is an INDEPENDENT event append with its own acquisition, so\nretrying an acquisition lands *that* event and can never replay the STATUS event. Opting\n`event_append.py` in also makes the completion-signature append survive contention, which is the\ndirect cause of the observed \"closed WITHOUT a completion signature\" warning at\n`transition_close.py:440` (exit 0, close already durable).\n\n1. `acquire()` and `write_lock()` gain **`retries: int = 0`**. The default of 0 reproduces today's\n   behaviour exactly, so every caller not listed below is unchanged with no edit. On an expired\n   pass the loop sleeps a jittered backoff and re-attempts, up to `retries` extra passes.\n2. Opted-in sites pass `_write_path_retries()`, reading env **`REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES`** (int, default\n   **2**, clamped `[0,10]`). `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES=0` restores today's fail-fast. Opted in, the write\n   path ceiling becomes ~180s, riding out the measured 70s holder.\n3. The terminating `LockTimeout` names the **cumulative** wait plus the holder; each exhausted pass\n   logs a warning naming the holder.\n4. `txn._acquire_write_lock` (`txn.py:84-86`) currently discards both by re-raising a generic\n   `CommandError(\"Error: could not acquire lock\")`. It propagates `str(exc)` instead, so the honest\n   message survives on the claim/transition path — the verb measured failing first.\n\n## Scope\n\n**Edited, opting in to retries:**\n- `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` — `retries` param, retry loop, `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES` helper,\n  cumulative-wait message, per-pass warning.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` — the canonical write path; `write_lock()` at **382, 420,\n  532** (`stage_and_commit`, `delete_events`). This is the mechanism behind `rebar comment` and is\n  what the ceiling claim is about.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/txn.py` — `_acquire_write_lock` (**84**) opts in and propagates the message.\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py` — **664** (locked commit-and-push) is a genuine write and opts in;\n  **375** (advisory push-retry merge) stays fail-fast.\n- `tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py` (new); `docs/concurrency.md`.\n\n**Deliberately NOT edited — every other `acquire()`/`write_lock()` caller keeps fail-fast via the\n`retries=0` default:** `compact_txn.py:340` and `compact_rebuild.py:126` (retries here would undo\n7084's R3 stand-aside and re-create the 48s holder that caused this bug); `fsck_repair.py:241` and\n`s3_doctor.py:199` (operator-driven repair — failing fast surfaces contention);\n`inbound_translate.py:283` (already retried at its advisory-lock layer); `sync.py:255`,\n`push.py:375`, `ensures.py:158` (best-effort advisory sweeps).\n\n## Testing\n\n- **Happy path:** an uncontended `acquire(retries=2)` wins on the first pass and never sleeps.\n- **Reproduction (RED→GREEN):** a real subprocess holder held past one budget, waiter budget\n  shorter than the hold. With `retries=0` the waiter raises `LockTimeout` (today's loss); with\n  `retries=2` it acquires on a later pass and its write is present. Scaled to seconds.\n- **No double-append:** after a contended acquire that succeeds on a later pass, exactly ONE event\n  is appended — proving the retry never replays the caller's write body.\n- **Exhaustion:** a holder outliving all passes still raises `LockTimeout` (fails loudly, does not\n  hang) with the cumulative wait in the message.\n- **Claim path:** a claim-shaped acquire behind an over-budget holder succeeds on a later pass; its\n  `CommandError` text carries the cumulative wait and holder.\n- **Env override:** `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES=0` restores single-budget fail-fast; out-of-range clamps.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Re-measured post-R1/R3/R5 main and recorded whether writes are still lost — done, numbers in\n      the AC#1 comment.\n- [ ] The failure-shape decision (retry-with-backoff over fair queueing) is recorded in Approach\n      with the evidence selecting it, verified by that section stating why FIFO does not address a\n      single over-budget holder.\n- [ ] A write whose first budget expires is re-attempted rather than discarded, verified by\n      `pytest -q tests/unit/test_lock_retry_zebrafish.py -k reproduction` exiting 0.\n- [ ] The retry never replays the caller's write body, verified by the no-double-append test\n      asserting an appended-event count of exactly 1.\n- [ ] A write exhausting every pass raises `LockTimeout` naming the cumulative wait, verified by\n      the exhaustion test asserting the message text.\n- [ ] `claim` succeeds on a later pass behind an over-budget holder, verified by the claim-path\n      test exiting 0.\n- [ ] `claim`'s error is no longer generic, verified by asserting the `CommandError` text contains\n      the cumulative wait and the holder.\n- [ ] Opted-in sites are exactly `event_append.py` (382/420/532), `txn.py` (84), `push.py` (664),\n      verified by `test -z \"$(grep -rn 'retries=' src/rebar --include='*.py' | grep -v '_store/lock.py' | grep -vE 'event_append|txn|push')\"`.\n- [ ] The `retries` default is 0 so unedited callers are unchanged, verified by a test asserting\n      `inspect.signature(lock.acquire).parameters['retries'].default == 0`.\n- [ ] `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES=0` restores single-budget fail-fast, verified by the env-override test.\n- [ ] Out-of-range `REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES` clamps to `[0,10]`, verified by the clamp test.\n- [ ] `docs/concurrency.md` documents the ceiling and the override, verified by\n      `grep -qE '^\\s*.?REBAR_LOCK_RETRIES.?' docs/concurrency.md`.\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0.\n- [ ] `make typecheck` exits 0.\n- [ ] `tests/integration/test_store_concurrency.py` passes unchanged.\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_store/lock.py` stays under the 800-line cap, verified by\n      `test \"$(wc -l < src/rebar/_store/lock.py)\" -lt 800`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786519073059535001,"uuid":"17acd5fe-b624-41e6-ba20-0eaef9fb9627"}